  Rust monsters are much less of a problem if you know they're coming.
They don't do any damage other than rusting worn items.  (None, zero,
zilch.  They can't damage you at all.)  So remove metal shields, gloves,
boots, and helms in advance.  Be sure rustable body armor is covered by
a cloak.

  Don't use a rustable weapon to attack them.  Elven dagger/broadsword
seem like a good idea.  Good strong pets would be even better.

  That's where means of detecting monsters at a distance is so
important:  Spell/potion of detect monster, telepathy with means of
self-blinding, lit levels, reconnaissance by fire, etc.

  Worst case you can put down a few dust Elbereths and let your pet(s)
get to work.  That would also let you take off the most important armor
at risk.  A non-cursed can of grease would be perfect, especially if
you're not careful about searching for rust traps.


